2 CONC Cantabria" as the sons of King Ervigio[377].  The primary sources on which these statements are based are not specified.  The table includes numerous errors and the information should therefore be viewed with caution.  The Chronic
2 CONC le of Alfonso III describes his son, Alfonso I King of Asturias, as "of the royal line" without specifying his ancestry[378].  The Historia Silense names "Petrus ex Recaredi…Gotorum principis progenie"[379], although Pedro's desce
2 CONC nt from King Recaredo I cannot be established.  It is assumed that this alleged family relationship with the Visigoths is another example of an invention by later genealogists wishing to fill the information gaps left by the prima
2 CONC ry sources.  Duque de Cantabria[380].] 
