2 CONT Guterre Mendes ( Spanish : Gutierre Menéndez ; ca. 870 [ 1 ] ) – m. [ 2 ] ) was a Galician nobleman and magnate .
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Hermenegildo Guterres , count of Coimbra and of Ermesinda Gatones , [ 3 ] daughter of Gatón , count of O Bierzo and of Egilona. He ruled as a lieutenant over six counties ( conmissa ) in Galicia , [ 4 ] some shared with his
2 CONC  brother Arias, [ 5 ] [ 6 ] by concession from King Alfonso IV .
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the brother-in-law of the King of Galicia Ordonho II for having married the latter to his sister Queen Elvira Mendes . [ 7 ] He was the uncle of the King of Galicia Sancho Ordonhes and also of Kings Afonso IV and Ramiro II 
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT King Sancho Ordonhes would marry his granddaughter Queen Goto Moniz, daughter of Munio Guterres , and Ramiro II with his niece Queen Adosinda Guterres . He exercised important powers by delegation from Ordonho II and received, amo
2 CONC ng other orders, to refound the Monastery of Santo Estevo de Ribas de Sil .
2 CONT
2 CONT Guterres supported the sons of Ordonho II against the descendants of Froila, managing to oust Afonso Froilaz and bring Sancho Ordóñez to the throne of Galicia through the coronation in Santiago de Compostela by the 6th bishop of L
2 CONC ugo , Hermenegildo , who held the position between 653 and 656.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was also a stronghold of King Ramiro II who, shortly after being crowned, reconfirms the donations that had been made to Guterre Mendes by Alfonso III "the Great" and confirmed by the King of Galicia Sancho Ordóñez. These were 
2 CONC abundant goods confiscated from the rebel Witiza , penultimate king of the Visigoths , who reigned between 702 and 710.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around the year 890 he married one of the most important Galician aristocrats, Ilduara Eriz or (Santa Ilduara de Celanova). The union of both families meant the creation of one of the greatest territorial patrimonies of the High M
2 CONC iddle Ages kingdom of Galicia .
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived in Galicia, and in the Condado Portucalense , although it is in Galicia that his most important assets are found, where Portomarín stands out and especially Vila Nova dos Infantes , where his manor house , the family mano
2 CONC r, was located.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Index
2 CONT 1	marriage and offspring
2 CONT two	References
2 CONT 3	Bibliography
2 CONT 4	external links
2 CONT marriage and offspring
2 CONT He married Ilduara Eris (d. ca. 958), daughter of Ero Fernandes , Count of Lugo , [ 4 ] [ 5 ] by whom he had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Munio Guterres (died ca. 959/960), [ 8 ] [ 5 ] who married his cousin Elvira Árias , daughter of Count Árias Mendes [ 9 ] and Ermesenda Gundesíndes. They were the parents of Goto Moniz, the wife of King Sancho Ordonhes . [ 10 ]
2 CONT Rosendo de Celanova , (26 November 907 -1 March 977) [ 5 ] [ 4 ] known as Rosendo Guterres or just Saint Rosendo. He was bishop of Mondonhedo (925-950 and 955-958) and of Santiago de Compostela (968-977) and founder of the Monaste
2 CONC ry of São Salvador de Celanova , where he retired, [ 8 ] among other important functions.
2 CONT Fruela Guterres (died ca. 943), count, husband of Sarracina and ancestor of the House of Trava , succeeded his uncle Arias in several of his tenancies . [ 5 ] [ 4 ]
2 CONT Adosinda Guterres (died after 964), [ 11 ] [ 5 ] wife of Jimeno Díaz. After becoming a widow, she married Ramiro Mendes, [ 12 ] [ 13 ] likely the parents of Queen Velasquita Ramires, wife of King Vermudo II . [ 14 ]
2 CONT Ermesenda Guterres [ 5 ] [ 8 ] (died after 934) was married to the Count of Deza , Paio Gonçalves , son of Gonçalo Afonso Betote and Teresa Eris, [ 15 ] the founders of the Monastery of Carboeiro. [ 16 ] [ 8 ]
2 CONT References
