1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT GARCÍA Iñíguez ([810]-killed by Arabs [Lumberri] 882[57], bur Leire Monastery).  .. ... ....
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [firstly] '''URRACA''', daughter of ---.  An undated charter refers to a confirmation by “rex domnus Garcia et regina domna Urraca maiore”[61].  Her origin is not known.  Rodrigo Ximénez de Rada, writing in the first half 
2 CONC of the 13th century, records that "Enecho…Arista…filium Garsiam" married "Urracam, de Regio semine"[62].  Jaurgain suggests that "de Regio semine" should be interpreted as meaning "de la même race que lui" (based on his assumption
2 CONC  that the kings of Navarre were descended from the dukes of Gascony, about which there appears to be no proof) and that Urraca was "fille de [https://www.geni.com/people/Sanche-II-duc-de-Gascogne/6000000000424707328 Sanche-Sancion
2 CONC  duc de Vasconie]", although he cites no primary source which confirms this parentage[63].  Her origin is discussed by Salazar y Acha who suggests that she was a member of the Banu Qasi family, related to the second wife of Fruela
2 CONC  II King of Asturias, which would account for the introduction of the name Fortún into the family of the kings of Navarre[64].  
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAVARRE.htm#GarciaIIniguezdied882
2 CONT ------
2 CONT == [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garc%C3%ADa_%C3%8D%C3%B1iguez_of_Pamplona#Marriage_and_descendants Wikipedia] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT The identity of García's wife or wives is poorly documented, and has been subject to much speculation. An undated confirmation of an earlier lost charter refers to King García and Queen '''Urraca''' Mayor, and this is thought by s
2 CONC ome to refer to García Íñiguez and an otherwise unknown wife, '''Urraca'''. Based on her name alone and the fact that one of his sons' names was Fortún, a common name among the Banu Qasi dynasty, it has been argued that Urraca cou
2 CONC ld have been ''{by https://www.geni.com/people/Fort%C3%BAn-ibn-Musa-val%C3%AD-de-Huesca/6000000001699492470}'' a granddaughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Musa-Ibn-Musa-lbn-Qasaw-Wal%C3%AD-de-Tudela-y-Huesca-y-Zaragoza/6000000
2 CONC 012263275369?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1606832998728&through=6000000012263275369 Musa ibn Musa ibn Qasi], the leader of the Banu Qasi clan.[8] Other historians have suggested alternative parentage, or suggested the document does no
2 CONC t refer to García Íñiguez at all but instead to García Sánchez II of Pamplona and his mother Queen Urraca Fernández. A second possible wife is infanta Leodegundia, daughter of Ordoño I of Asturias. She is known to have married a r
2 CONC uler of Pamplona not named in the primary source, and García Íñiguez is one of those speculated to have been this prince.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT García Íñiguez had following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Fortún Garcés, King of Pamplona from 870 until 905 and married to Auria.
2 CONT *Onneca Garcés, married to Aznar Galíndez II, Count of Aragon.[9]
2 CONT *Sancho Garcés, father of Aznar Sánchez de Larraun — the second husband of his cousin Onneca Fortúnez — and probably of Velazquita, who married Mutarrif ibn Musa, of the Banu Qasi.[a]
2 CONT
