2 TITL Proposta de árvore genealógica da Casa de Vímara Peres
1 NOTE First count of Portugal. Warlord of the 9th century in what once was west Iberia.
2 CONT Vimara, also known as Vimerano, was a vassal of the King of Asturias, Leon and Galicia, Alfonso III. Vimara Peres was sent to reconquer lands from the Berber Moors who had invaded Visigothic Hispania. He established the first coun
2 CONC ty of Condado da Portucale north of the Douro River. Vimara Peres founded the town of Vimar Guimaranis present day Guimaraes. Vimara Peres 0873 in Guimaraes. His son, Lucidio Vimaranes took over and the dynasty lasted until 1071 w
2 CONC hen Count Nuno Mendes was defeated at the battle of Pedroso by King Garcia II of Galicia; after which he became King Garcia II of Galicia and Portugal. The name Pedroso means, Land of Pedro. or Land of Peres.
2 CONT Vimara served as king from 820 through 873.
2 CONT 1: Collins, Roger. Visigothic Spain, 409-711.
2 CONT Blackwell publishing 2004.
2 CONT 2: King, P.D., King Chindasuinth and the first territorial law code of the Visigothic kingdon.
2 CONT Edward James-Oxford-Clarendon Press 1980, PP. 131-157.
