2 CONT Galindo II Aznárez fue Conde de Aragón (893-922), sucediendo a su padre Aznar II Galíndez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrocinó el golpe de estado de Pamplona (905), del que resultó el cambio de la dinastía pamplonesa por otra rama más favorable a los intereses de Aragón.
2 CONT
2 CONT Se casó dos veces: con Sancha Garcés y con Acibella Garcés. Tuvo dos hijas: Toda, casada con Hunfredo Bernat, conde de Ribagorza, y Andregoto Galíndez (condesa 922-925), casada con García Sánchez I, rey de Navarra (925-970)
2 CONT
2 CONT Murió en 922.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Galindo Aznárez II From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Galindo Aznárez II (d. 922) was a Count of Aragón (893-922), the son and successor of Aznar Galíndez II. Galindo sponsored the 905 coup d'etat in Pamplona, with the change of the Pamplonese dynasty to another branch allied to Arag
2 CONC ón. Galindo was married twice. By his first wife, Acibella Garcés of Gascony, daughter of Count García II Sánchez of Gascony, he had sons Miro and Bishop Redemtus, along with daughter Toda, wife of Hunifred Bernat, count of Ribago
2 CONC rza, to whom she brought Sobrarbe. By his second wife, Sancha Garcés of Pamplona, daughter of 'king' García Jiménez, he had Velasquita and Andregota Galíndez (countess 922-925), who married García Sanchez, king of Pamplona (925-97
2 CONC 0). He also sired several illegitimate sons: Guntoslo, Sancho, Belasco, Banzo, and Aznar. The first of these, Guntoslo, is apparently the man of this name who would later be count of Aragon, but with none of the autonomy shown by 
2 CONC his ancestors, being a fully subservient vassal of his brother-in-law the king of Pamplona.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Galindo Aznárez II (d. 922) was a Count of Aragón (893-922), the son and successor of Aznar Galíndez II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Galindo sponsored the 905 coup d'etat in Pamplona, with the change of the Pamplonese dynasty to another branch allied to Aragón.
2 CONT
2 CONT Galindo was married twice. By his first wife, Acibella Garcés of Gascony, daughter of Count García II Sánchez of Gascony, he had sons Miro and Bishop Redemtus, along with daughter Toda, wife of Hunifred Bernat, count of Ribagorza,
2 CONC  to whom she brought Sobrarbe. By his second wife, Sancha Garcés of Pamplona, daughter of 'king' García Jiménez, he had Velasquita and Andregota Galíndez (countess 922-925), who married García Sanchez, king of Pamplona (925-970). 
2 CONC He also sired several illegitimate sons: Guntoslo, Sancho, Belasco, Banzo, and Aznar. The first of these, Guntoslo, is apparently the man of this name who would later be count of Aragon, but with none of the autonomy shown by his 
2 CONC ancestors, being a fully subservient vassal of his brother-in-law the king of Pamplona.
2 CONT --------------------
