1 NOTE {geni:about_me} m ONECA, daughter of --- (-before 959).  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 25 Aug 951 under which “Scemenus et Adosinda” donated property to Celanova “iermano nostro et pontifici nostro Rudesindo episc
2 CONC opo” which is signed by “Scemenus Didaci et Onnice prolis, Adosinda Guttierrici et Ilduare prolis”[637].  According to Pérez de Urbel[638], she may have been Onega Jiménez, daughter of Jimeno --- & his wife Leodegundia de Navarra.
2 CONC   "Honecca…cum filiis meis Munna, Ledegundia, Exemenus et Mummadonna" donated property to the monastery of Lorvão by charter dated 5 Dec 928, subscribed by "Honneca, Munnia, Ledegundia, Exemenus Didaz, Mummadomna, Aloytus Lucidi, 
2 CONC Roderigus Tedoniz, Ermegildus Gundisaluiz, Gundesindus Didaz…"[639]. 
2 CONT
