2 CONT
2 CONT Abdullah ibn Muhammad (عبد الله بن محمد; January 11, 844 - October 15, 912) of the Umayyad dynasty, was the seventh Emir of Córdoba, reigning from 888 to 912 in the Al-Andalus (Moorish Iberia).
2 CONT
2 CONT The most formidable threat for the emir was Umar Ibn Hafsun, who had conquered the provinces of Rayyo (including Bobastro), Elvira (including Granada) and Jaén, and had allied with the populations of Archidona, Baeza, Úbeda and Pr
2 CONC iego. In 891 Ibn Hafsun was defeated near the castle of Polei and lost several cities; Abdullah after the victory massacred all the Christians, while the Muslims of the conquered cities were pardoned. However, by the following yea
2 CONC r Ibn Hafsun had already recovered, and conquered back all the lost territories.
2 CONT
2 CONT The emir signed a peace with Ibn Hafsun (who had allied with the Banu Qasi family, controlling the Ebro valley, and the Kingdom of Asturias) in 901; the war however broke out again the following year, only to be halted by the deat
2 CONC h at Córdoba of Abdullah, who was improving his positions. The son he has designed as successor was killed by one of Abdullah's brothers. The latter was in turn executed by Abdullah's father, who named as successor Abd ar-Rahman I
2 CONC II, son of the killed son of Abdullah.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Altamira, Rafael (1999). "Il califfato occidentale". Storia del mondo medievale. II. pp. 477–515. 
2 CONT
