2 CONC la Peña in 987, he titled himself "King of Navarre," the first time that title had been used. In other places, he appears as the first King of Aragon and in others the third. These titles, however, did not come into common usage u
2 CONC ntil the late eleventh century. The epithet "Abarca," meaning "sandal," is not contemporary, but is medieval.
