1 NOTE The Aragón of 1035 was created at the death of Sancho III Garces, King ofNavarre, Emperor of Spain.  Navarre, the patrimony, was passed to hiseldest son Garcia, Castile (acquired as a county through Sancho's wife)went to Fernando 
2 CONC (the favorite, who through his marriage to the heiressof Leon/Asturias became king of the biggest chunk), teen age Gonzalo gotthe counties of Sorbrabe and Ribagorza (the claim to which also came toSancho through Castile), while hi
2 CONC s bastard Ramiro was given Aragón, whichhad it's origins in a County of Aragón dating to the 9th century whichcame to Navarre through the marriage of Sancho's great-grandfather.Ramiro was to be vassal of Garcia, but in a series of
2 CONC  squabbles in thefollowing
2 CONT years, he first threw off his brother's overlordship, and the absorbedGonzalo's territories (Gonzalo having died under mysteriouscircumstances). In the following generation, Sancho Ramirez was able totake control of the Kingdom of
2 CONC  Navarre following the murder of its king,Sancho IV Garces, (the western portion of that kingdom falling to theKing de Castile, cousin Sancho Fernandez, hence Menendez Pidal's 'War ofthe Three Sanchos'). This was held by two sons 
2 CONC of Sancho Ramirez, but waslost when both died without surviving issue, and a third brother, Ramiro
2 CONT II was reluctantly recalled from a monastery. He married, had a daughterPetronilla, and engaged the infant to the adult Count of Barcelona,immediately returning to the monastic life. Petronilla's son Alfonso IIinherited both terri
2 CONC tories. Thus the Aragón of 1035 was little more thanthe mountain county of the 9th century, and it was an
2 CONT agressive policy of the first several generations which brought about thekingdom of status.[Custer February 1, 2002 Family Tree.FTW]
2 CONT
