2 CONT [https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garc%C3%ADa_Jiménez_de_Pamplona '''García Jiménez'''] (835-after 885) from Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Códice de Roda shows García Jiménez to have married twice, firstly to '''Oneca''', "Rebel of Sangüesa" with whom he had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Íñigo''', called 'king' in the Códice de Roda when reporting his marriage to a granddaughter of Fortún Garcés of Pamplona, but not in his own entry as son of García Jiménez. He perhaps succeeded to his father's sub-kingdom (e
2 CONC lse the term is being used as an honorific rather than a title).
2 CONT # '''Sancha''', married as her first husband Íñigo Fortúnez, son of king Fortún Garcés of Pamplona, and subsequently remarried to Galindo Aznárez II, Count of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
