2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         [MUNIO Muñoz (-[17 Jan 1097/21 Mar 1097]).  The dating clause of a charter dated 17 Jan 1097, under which "Vermudo Godestez" donated property in Rimor to the monastery of San Pedro de Montes, names "Monnio Monniz impera
2 CONC nte ipsa terra de Ulver"[879].  His supposed sister "Xemena Munniz" is named in dating clauses of charters of the same monastery, both before the date of this document and from 21 Mar 1097 (see above).  This suggests that Munio ma
2 CONC y have returned from elsewhere in [1095/96] to assume his heritage but died soon afterwards without leaving direct heirs.] 
