2 CONT * < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Ansúrez Wikipedia] > '''Pedro Ansúrez''' (floruit 1065–1117;[2] died probably 9 September 1118[3]) was a Castilian nobleman, count of Liébana, Saldaña and Carrión in the closing decades of 
2 CONC the eleventh century and the opening decades of the twelfth. He is considered the founder and first lord of Valladolid. Pedro was a descendant of the Beni Gómez family of Castilian nobility, the son of Ansur Díaz, by his first wif
2 CONC e, whose name is unknown.[4] His grandfather, Diego Fernández, was a count of Saldaña and Carrión. 
