1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MOORISH%20SPAIN.htm#_ftnref450<br/>
2 CONT 2.         ISMAIL ibn Musa (-Monzón 10 Oct 889, bur Monzón).  Al-Udri records that "en algunos Anales" record that "Musa ibn Musa" was survived by "varios hijos…Lubb, Ismail, Mutarrif y Fortun", adding that Ismail was "gobernador…
2 CONC de Zaragoza"[451].  He captured Zaragoza 16 Jan 872[452].  Al-Udri records that "Ismail [ibn Musa]" entered Huesca, killed [his father-in-law] "Abd Allah ibn Jalaf ibn Rasid" and "todos sus hijos", and captured "de su villa, Barba
2 CONC stro…Alquézar y de toda la Barbitaniya"[453].  The Chronicon Albeldense records that “Zmael Iben Muiza” defended “Cæsaraugustam” [Zaragoza] against the attack of “Almundar, Mahomat regis filius” in 882[454].  The Chronicon Albelde
2 CONC nse records that “Ababdella, filius Jub” allied himself with Emir al-Mundhir and was attacked by “tius suus Zmael et suus congermanus…Zmael Ibem Furtum” whom he captured and imprisoned in Viguera castle in [882][455].  After Muham
2 CONC mad broke relations with the Emir, Ismail was released and transferred the castle of Valtierra to Muhammad in return[456].  Al-Udri records that "Muhammad ibn Lubb" captured "Ismail ibn Musa y a sus primos [corrected by the transl
2 CONC ator to "sobrinos"]…Ismail et Lubb hijos estos dos de Fortun ibn Musa" at "Calahorra…el viernes 10 de yumada II" A.H. 270 [15 Nov 883] and freed them only after "Zaragoza, Tudela y Valtierra" were transferred to him, although he s
2 CONC ent Ismail ibn Musa "al castillo de Monzón" where he remained until his death "el 10 de yumada II" A.H. 276 [10 Oct 889] and where he was buried[457].  Ibn Hayyan records that "Ismail hijo de Muza, de la familia de los Benicasi, s
2 CONC eñor de Lérida" relinquished his position in favour of "sus dos hijos, Muza y Motárrif" and died soon afterwards, dated A. H. 276 [6 May 889/25 Apr 890][458].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (x) SAYYIDA, daughter of ABD ALLAH ibn Jalaf ibn Rasid.  Al-Udri records that "Ismail [ibn Musa]" patched up an alliance with "Abd Allah ibn Jalaf ibn Rasid" and married "su hija Sayyida"[459]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ismail had three children by unknown mothers: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         MUSA ibn Ismail (-killed in battle Barbotania [6 May 889/25 Apr 890]).  Ibn Hazm names "Muhammad…Musa…y Said" as the sons of "Ismail ibn Musa", adding that Musa was killed "en Huesca"[460].  Ibn Hayyan records that "Is
2 CONC mail hijo de Muza, de la familia de los Benicasi, señor de Lérida" relinquished his position in favour of "sus dos hijos, Muza y Motárrif" who were ambushed by "Atauil rey de Huesca" while defending "su distrito de Barbotania", wh
2 CONC en Musa was killed and Motarrif captured, dated A. H. 276 [6 May 889/25 Apr 890][461]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         MUTARIF ibn Ismail .  Ibn Hayyan records that "Ismail hijo de Muza, de la familia de los Benicasi, señor de Lérida" relinquished his position in favour of "sus dos hijos, Muza y Motárrif" who were ambushed by "Atauil r
2 CONC ey de Huesca" while defending "su distrito de Barbotania", when Musa was killed and Motarrif captured, dated A. H. 276 [6 May 889/25 Apr 890][462]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *c)         SAID ibn Ismail .  Ibn Hazm names "Muhammad…Musa…y Said" as the sons of "Ismail ibn Musa", adding that Said died "en Córdoba"[463]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ismail & his (x) wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *d)         MUHAMMAD ibn Ismail .  Al-Udri records the birth of "Muhammad", son of "Ismail [ibn Musa]" and his wife "Sayyida"[464].  Ibn Hazm names "Muhammad…Musa…y Said" as the sons of "Ismail ibn Musa", adding that Muhammad was 
2 CONC "rey de Toledo" and was killed by the inhabitants of Toledo[465].  Muhammad had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          LUBB ibn Muhammad .  Ibn Hazm names "Lubb, que se reunió con el sii en Ifriqiya" as the son of "Muhammad ibn Ismail, el que fue asesinado en Toledo"[466]. 
