2 CONT García Jiménez (835 - ?) fue hijo del Duque Jimeno de Pamplona. Nació en la región de los Pirineos que hoy corresponde a Navarra, donde su familia tenía sus dominios.
2 CONT
2 CONT De su matrimonio con Onneca, "Rebelle de Sangüesa", fue padre de Sancha Garcés de Pamplona, quien desposó al conde Galindo II Aznárez de Aragón, y de Íñigo Garcés. Su segundo matrimonio fue con Dadildis de Pallars (hija de Lupo de
2 CONC  Bigorra y una hija del Conde de Toulouse, Ramón I) con quien tuvo a quien sería el primer rey de Navarra de la dinastía Jimena, Sancho Garcés I de Navarra, y Jimeno Garcés de Navarra.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT García Jiménez or García II was (sub- or co-)king of a part of Pamplona in the late 9th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Basque ruling dynasty (Jiménez) was apparently in control of a part of what would become the kingdom of Navarre distinct from that held by the descendants of Iñigo Arista. García presumably succeeded his father during the life
2 CONC time of García Íñiguez, and is listed by the Códice de Roda as being of "another part of the kingdom" of Pamplona.
2 CONT
2 CONT By a popular reconstruction, when King García I supposedly died in 870 while his son and heir Fortún Garcés was imprisoned in Córdoba, García Jiménez is said to have become uncontested regent of the kingdom until he was killed at 
2 CONC Aybar (882) in a battle against the Emir of Córdoba. However, there is evidence that García Íñiguez was still living at the time of his son's return in 880, and it may well have been that monarch who was killed in 882. In fact, th
2 CONC ere is no documentary evidence of García Jiménez playing any role in the government of the greater kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT García Jiménez married firstly to Oneca, "Rebel of Sangüesa" with whom he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Íñigo, called 'king' in the Roda Codex, perhaps his father's successor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha, married as her first husband Íñigo Fortúnez, son of king Fortún of Pamplona, and remarried Galindo Aznárez II, Count of Aragon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT García Jiménez married secondly Dadildis de Pallars, sister of count Raymond I of Pallars and Ribagorza, with whom he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho, later sole king of Pamplona. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jimeno, king in succession to Sancho.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
