1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sancho Ramírez (before 1043 – 1105/November 1110) was an illegitimate son of King Ramiro I of Aragon and Amuña, the firstborn and brother of his namesake who would inherit the throne and reign as Sancho Ramírez.[1]
2 CONC [2][a]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancho_Ram%C3%ADrez,_Count_of_Ribagorza
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Beatriz, whose patronymic is not recorded in any medieval document, and appears with her in an 1100 charter from the town of Uncastillo confirming the sale made by their deceased son Pedro to a certain "don Juan".[11] I
2 CONC n November 1110, the now-widowed Beatriz made a donation to the Monastery of San Vicente in Roda de Isábena of some salt mines that she received from her brother-in-law, King Sancho Ramírez.[c] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Four children were born of this marriage:
2 CONT *García Sánchez, Lord of Aibar, Atarés and Javierrelatre, married to Teresa Cajal, sister of Fortún Garcés Cajal. They were the parents of Pedro de Atarés who was a claimant to the throne of Aragon after the death of Alfonso the B
2 CONC attler;[9]
2 CONT *Pedro Sánchez (died before 1100);[11][12]
2 CONT *Talesa Sánchez, the wife of Gaston IV, Viscount of Bearn;[9]
2 CONT *Beatriz Sánchez.[9]
