1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AQUITAINE.htm#AgnesMRamiroIAragon
2 CONT
2 CONT a)        ''' [AGNES de Poitou''' .  Agnes was the daughter of Duke Guillaume VI according to Szabolcs de Vajay, although he cites no source in support of this[455].  According to Richard, Duke Guillaume VI died childless[456].  A
2 CONC gnes is shown as the possible daughter of Duke Guillaume VII "l'Aigret" in Europäische Stammtafeln[457], marrying Pierre I Comte de Savoie as her second husband although she would have been only about six years old at the time of 
2 CONC her supposed first marriage with Ramiro King of Aragon.  From an onomastic point of view, it is surprising that a daughter of Duke Guillaume VI would have been named Agnes, a name which appears to have been introduced into the fam
2 CONC ily of the Comtes de Poitou only after the third marriage of Duke Guillaume V to Agnes de Mâcon.  The primary source which confirms her marriage to King Ramiro has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1054] ) as his second wife, RAMIRO I King of Aragon, illegitimate son of SANCHO III King of Navarre & his mistress Sancha de Aibar (Aibar [1008]-killed in battle Graus 8 May 1063, bur Monastery of San Juan de la Peña).'
2 CONC '']''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnes_of_Aquitaine,_Countess_of_Savoy#Possible_wife_of_Ramiro_I_of_Aragon
2 CONT
2 CONT [ could be her cousin https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-of-Aquitaine-countess-of-Savoy/6000000010667918576 wife in 1064 to https://www.geni.com/people/Pietro-I-conte-di-Savoia/6000000000437316601 ]
