1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garcia_Arnaldo_di_Bigorre
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bigorra was a feudal jurisdiction of Aquitaine in the region of Tarba (Tarbes), which took its name from a castle. Bigorra (Bigorre in French) is a region of Gascony, which today occupies part of the department of Hautes-Pyrénées 
2 CONC (France) extending from the Pyrenees to the plain of Tarba. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT García Arnaldo, comte de Bigorre1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 972
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Arnaldo I, comte de Bigorre b. circa 950
2 CONT
2 CONT Charts	Descendants of Charlemage
2 CONT
2 CONT      García Arnaldo, comte de Bigorre was born circa 972. He was the son of Arnaldo I, comte de Bigorre. García Arnaldo, comte de Bigorre married Ricar d' Astarac, daughter of Guillermo I d' Astarac.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Ricar d' Astarac b. circa 975
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT Gersinde, comtesse de Bigorre+ b. c 995, d. a 10382
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 227-34.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1265] Genealogy.eu, online genealogy.euweb.cz, Counts of Bigorre, Ribagorza and Pailhars.
