1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''PLEASE DON'T FOLLOW THE MedLands LINE-UP GIVEN BELOW.'''
2 CONT * It is kept here for reference, but the charters don't substantiate some of the connections. It seems far better to follow Pavillet in his "Histoire Généaligique de la Maison de Villeneuve en Languedoc" (referenced under the Douc
2 CONC ments section).
2 CONT * In addition, MedLands does not list Wachaire as a son of Mayeul - even though it references him ("Walchario"). Wachaire is key for this line-up, as he is the head of the "de Villeneuve" descendants throughout the Languedoc and t
2 CONC he Provence (see Pavillet for further detail).
2 CONT * This is a curated profile. Please get in touch if corrections need to be made on new evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================================
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT VICOMTES de NARBONNE [900]-924
2 CONT
2 CONT MAYEUL [Maiolus] [I], son of --- (-before 15 Jun 911).  Vicomte de Narbonne.  m RAYMONDE, daughter of --- (-[before 15 Jun 911]).  A charter dated 15 Jun 911, under which Arnust Archibishop of Narbonne donated property to Saint-Pa
2 CONC ul de Narbonne, names "infantes Majolo vicecomite et uxori suæ Raymundæ...Walchario et...Albericho vicecomite", the wording implying that the parents were deceased at that date[562].  Settipani suggests that she was the daughter o
2 CONC f Raymond I Comte de Toulouse[563].  Maieul [I] & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GAUTHIER .  A charter dated 15 Jun 911, under which Arnust Archibishop of Narbonne donated property to Saint-Paul de Narbonne, names "infantes Majolo vicecomite et uxori suæ Raymundæ...Walchario et...Albericho vicecomit
2 CONC e", the wording implying that the parents were deceased at that date[564].  Vicomte de Narbonne.  m ---.  The name of Gauthier's wife is not known.  Gauthier & his wife had [two] children:   
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          RAYMONDE .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m FOUCHER Seigneur de Valensole {Alpes-de-Haute-Provence}, son of ---.  Raymonde & her husband had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       MAYEUL (-Aug 993).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  [A charter dated 4 May 948 noted obligations to Cluny of “Vualterius” relating to property “in villa Verchesoni et in Galn
2 CONC a seu in Petrolio”, in the presence of “Vualterium vicecomitem…et monachi…Maiolus”[565].  No proof has been found that this monk was the future abbot of Cluny but this looks probable.]  Abbot of Cluny [948].  “Abbas Maiolus” is na
2 CONC med for the first time in a charter dated [948/49][566].  He is last named in a charter dated Aug 993[567]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         [MAYEUL [III] (-after 24 Oct 946).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Vicomte de Narbonne.  "Maiolus vicecomes" donated property "Ursum…situs super fluvio Urbione intra paga 
2 CONC Carcassonne et Narbonense" to the abbey of Lagrasse for the souls of "patris mei et matris meæ et uxoris mæ Ranilone et…alia uxore mea quæ fuit quondam…Estuer et pro filiabus meis et pro filiis meis Simplicio et Vuadamiro" by char
2 CONC ter dated 24 Oct 946[568].]  m firstly ESTHER, daughter of ---.  "Maiolus vicecomes" donated property to the abbey of Lagrasse for the souls of "…alia uxore mea quæ fuit quondam…Estuer…" by charter dated 24 Oct 946[569].  m second
2 CONC ly RANILO, daughter of ---.  "Maiolus vicecomes" donated property to the abbey of Lagrasse for the souls of "…uxoris mæ Ranilone…" by charter dated 24 Oct 946[570].  Maieul [II] & his [first/second] wife had [four or more] childre
2 CONC n: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       SIMPLICE .  "Maiolus vicecomes" donated property to the abbey of Lagrasse "…pro filiabus meis et pro filiis meis Simplicio et Vuadamiro" by charter dated 24 Oct 946[571]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (b)       VUADIMIRE .  "Maiolus vicecomes" donated property to the abbey of Lagrasse "…pro filiabus meis et pro filiis meis Simplicio et Vuadamiro" by charter dated 24 Oct 946[572]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (c)       daughters .  "Maiolus vicecomes" donated property to the abbey of Lagrasse "…pro filiabus meis et pro filiis meis Simplicio et Vuadamiro" by charter dated 24 Oct 946[573].  
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         AUBRY [Alberic] ([880/90]-[10 Sep] 945, bur Besançon Saint-Etienne).  A charter dated 15 Jun 911, under which Arnust Archibishop of Narbonne donated property to Saint-Paul de Narbonne, names "infantes Majolo vicecomite 
2 CONC et uxori suæ Raymundæ...Walchario et...Albericho vicecomite", the wording implying that the parents were deceased at that date[574].  A genealogy of the Comtes de Mâcon, included in the cartulary of Saint-Vincent de Mâcon, names "
2 CONC Albericus Narbonensis" and his marriage to "filiam Raculfi vicecomitis post mortem domini Bernonis Matiscensis episcopi", after which he made himself first Comte de Mâcon[575]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         [MAYEUL [II] (-[Jun 949/20 Apr 950]).  Vicomte de Mâcon.  The parentage of Vicomte Mayeul is not known, but it looks like that he was an otherwise unknown younger brother of Aubry Comte de Mâcon.  However, his name, as 
2 CONC well as the use of the names Gauthier, Raymonde and Aubry among his descendnants, indicates a close connection with the family of the vicomtes de Narbonne.  From a chronological point of view, it is likely that he was of the same 
2 CONC generation as Aubry Comte de Mâcon.  It would also make sense that Comte Aubry appointed his younger brother as his vicomte in Mâcon.  It does not appear likely that Mayeul [II] was the same person as shown above as Mayeul [III], 
2 CONC as a charter names the wife of Mayeul [II] as Landrada, whereas another charter names the two wives of Mayeul [III] as shown above.  Vicomte Mayeul is named in an undated charter relating to the inheritance of Landry, in the cartu
2 CONC lary of Saint-Vincent de Mâcon[576].  Vicomte Mayeul subscribed a charter dated to 936 relating to Saint-Vincent de Mâcon[577].]  
