2 NICK M. Ardzrouni
2 NICK Princesa de Vaspurakan da Armenia
1 NAME Unnamed Armenian princess
1 SEX F
1 OCCU Princesa de Vaspurakan da Armenia
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Two sources, the ''Livro Velho das Linhagens'' and the ''Fragmento'' both tell the story of an unnamed Armenian princess who, during her pilgrimage to Compostela in Spain, was kidnapped and raped by Mendo Alão, sen
2 CONC hor da Vila de Bragança
2 CONT
2 CONT Now, as to whether this story is true, we simply do not know. It was common practice for these noble families to fabricate fantastical and exotic ancient ancestors for their families. Through this unfortunate princess, they could 
2 CONC claim to be the descendants of kings. There is unfortunately no way to verify these legends.
2 CONT
2 CONT As for the identity of her parents, the sources do not tell us anything. She is simply identified as an Armenian princess.
2 CONT
2 CONT The problem is that during this period, there were multiple kingdoms in Armenia, and there is no indication as to which dynasty she is supposed to belong to. There are no references to her from Armenian sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT The genealogist Narciso Binayan Carmona tries to identify her parentage in an article titled "Una princesa armenia en Compostela en el siglo XI: su genealogia."
2 CONT
2 CONT He states that he believes that the story is true, but does not offer any proof for this belief or explain why he thinks so.
2 CONT
2 CONT If we accept that she is not a legendary person, the problem is that there were 5 different kingdoms in Armenia during the 11th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of his article is devoted to setting up the background for Armenian history and has little to do with the princess. He concludes that in his estimation, the best candidate for her parentage comes from the kingdom of Vaspuraka
2 CONC n, since they had contacts with Byzantium during this period. He concludes that perhaps she is a relative, maybe a daughter, of Johannes II, King of Vaspurakan the ruler of Vaspurakan during the period of her supposed pilgrimage.
2 CONT
2 CONT But, he has no evidence for this connection, it is just a guess. It represents an interesting theory, but it is simply that, a theory. There is not enough evidence for it to be represented as fact on the Geni tree and I (Tamas Cal
2 CONC dwell-Gilbert) suggest that the connection between the princess and Johannes II, King of Vaspurakan be removed. The connection is not based on sources. His argument is interesting, but it certainly does not rule out any of the oth
2 CONC er Armenian kingdoms, let alone come close to proving that she existed in the first place. We could include a discussion in their about sections for the theory though.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometimes identified as Princess of Vaspurakan, Armenia, Ne Artsrouni, Joana Romães Arcruni of Armenia, but there is no evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Ne Ardzrouní) Pais
2 CONT
2 CONT Senek'erim Hovhannes Artsrouni, roi de Vaspourakan +1026 Kouschkousch Bagratid Casamentos e filhos
2 CONT
2 CONT Casada cerca 1025 com D. Mendo Alaniz, tiveram Ourroana Menendez ca 1025 D. Fernando Mendes «o Velho» de Bragançãos ca 1030-ca 1117 Notas
2 CONT
2 CONT Foi raptada por seu futuro marido quando, cerca de 1025, ficou instalada no mosteiro de Castro de Avelãs (Bragança), numa peregrinação que fazia a Santiago de Compostela.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fontes: Manuel Abranches de Soveral («Os Bragançãos», Lisboa 2004, de J. C. L. S. Machado)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Princesa de Vaspurakan.  Habría sido raptada por su futuro marido, Mendo Alao, mientras acompañaba a su padre (Rey de Vaspurakan) en una peregrinación a Santiago de Compostela desde su país, más allá del Mar Negro.  Algunos geneal
2 CONC ogistas dicen que se trata de una fábula.  Geneall la trata como verdadera, pero se equivoca casi desde el principio, confundiendo hermanos con padres.
