1 OCCU Infanta de Castilla
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CASTILE.htm#_ftnref556<br/>
2 CONT King Alfonso VI & his fifth wife had three children (born before the marriage of their parents): 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         Infanta doña SANCHA de Castilla y León ([1100/16 Mar 1104]-after 10 May 1125).  The Chronicon Regum Legionensium names "Sancha the wife of count Rodrigo and Elvira who married Duke Roger of Sicily" as the daughters of K
2 CONC ing Alfonso and his fourth "legitimate wife…Elisabeth"[563].  Both daughters are named in a charter dated 16 Mar 1104[564].  In view of the dates of their marriages, it is unlikely that they were born much before this date.  This 
2 CONC suggests that their mother may have been King Alfonso's fifth wife, formerly known by her Muslim name Zaïda, although if their estimated birth dates are correct there would have been an interval of several years between their birt
2 CONC hs and the birth of their older brother Sancho, which seems surprising.  "Comite domno Roderico Gonzalvus cum uxore mea Sandecia prolis filia regis Adephonsus" donated the monastery of San Mames to Santa María de Piasca by charter
2 CONC  dated "mense Iulii, Era 1100" (misdated)[565].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1120 or 1122) as his first wife, RODRIGO González de Lara Señor de Lara y Liébana, son of GONZALO Núñez & his wife Goto --- (-after 1143).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta doña SANCHA de Castilla, daughter of don ALFONSO VI King of Castile and León & his fifth wife Isabel née Zaïda --- ([1120/16 Mar 1104]-after 10 May 1125).  The Chronicon Regum Legionensium names "Sancha the wife of count R
2 CONC odrigo and Elvira who married Duke Roger of Sicily" as the daughters of King Alfonso and his fourth "legitimate wife…Elisabeth"[995].  Both daughters are named in a charter dated 16 Mar 1104[996].  In view of the dates of their ma
2 CONC rriages, it is unlikely that they were born much before this date.  This suggests that their mother may have been King Alfonso's fifth wife, formerly known by her Muslim name Zaïda, although if their estimated birth dates are corr
2 CONC ect there would have been an interval of several years between their births and the birth of their older brother Sancho, which seems surprising.  m secondly (9 Sep 1135) as her second husband, doña ESTEFANIA de Urgel, widow of don
2 CONC  FERNANDO García [de Castro] Señor de Hita y Uceda, daughter of ARMENGOL [V] Conde de Urgel & his wife doña María Pérez Señora de Valladolid (-after 1143).  Rodrigo & his first wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             don PEDRO Rodríguez (-1180).  Pedro Rodríguez “filius comitis Ruderici Gonsaluez” transferred properties to the bishop of Burgos by charter dated Mar 1166[997].  m doña MENCIA López, daughter of don LOPE Díaz Conde 
2 CONC de Haro, Señor Soberano de Vizcaya & his second wife doña Aldonza Ruiz de Castro.  “Sancia Lopez…comitissa domna Mencia…Urraca Lopez…Aldonza Lopez…Elvira Lopez…Don Garcia Lopez…Stephania Lopez monacha…Tota Lopez…Maria Lopez…Diago 
2 CONC Lopez” donated property to the monastery of Santa María de Cañas by charter dated Sep 1174[998].  "Domna Alduenza cometissa…olim…domni Lupi comitis uxor" donated property to the monastery of San Millán de la Cogolla by charter dat
2 CONC ed 1187, witnessed by "domnus Didacus Lupiz, domna Mencia cometissa, domna Alduenza, domna Tota Camensis abbatissa, domnus Sancius Lupiz…"[999]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)             doña ELVIRA Rodríguez de Lara (-8 Aug 1159).  m (before 1135) as his second wife, ARMENGOL [VI] "el Castellano" Conde de Urgel, son of ARMENGOL [V] Conde de Urgel & his wife doña María Pérez Señora de Valladolid (Va
2 CONC lladolid 1096-28 Jun 1154, bur Nuestra Señora de Valbuena). 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)             daughter.  According to Reilly, two daughters had been born of Rodrigo's first marriage by 10 May 1125[1000].  However, Farmerie and Taylor say that don Pedro and doña Elvira were the only children of don Rodrigo Go
2 CONC nzález de Lara[1001].  Don Rodrigo González joined with "his daughters" by his first marriage in 1125 in a donation to the monastery of Vega[1002]. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Rodrigo I Fruelez, conde de Castilla1 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 730?, d. circa 800
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Fruela, duque de Cantabria1 b. circa 700?, d. 765 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also called Count Rodrigo I of Castile. Rodrigo I Fruelez, conde de Castilla was born circa 730?. He was the son of Fruela, duque de Cantabria.1 Rodrigo I Fruelez, conde de Castilla married Sancha (?).1 Count of Castile between 76
2 CONC 2 and 800.1 Rodrigo I Fruelez, conde de Castilla married Sancha de Gascogne, daughter of Lupus III, Duque de Vasconia. Rodrigo I Fruelez, conde de Castilla died circa 800.1 
