2 CONT '''DIEGO Jiménez de los Cameros''', son of JIMENO Iñíguez & his second wife Endulcia --- (-after 9 Oct 1184).  “Petrus Semenez” donated property to the monastery of Sacramenia by charter dated 19 Apr 1162, which names “Didaco frat
2 CONC re meo et Teresa sorore mea, eiusdemque marito Lupe de Mendoza”[253].  Alfonso VIII King of Castille granted the town of Herce, Rioja to "Didaco Semenez et uxori vestre domna Giomar et filiis et filiabus vestris" by charter dated 
2 CONC 9 Apr 1173[254].  “Didacus Ximenez cum uxore mea Guiomar et sororibus meis domna Urraca et domna Teressa, domna quoque Sanctia et domina Maria et cum omnibus filiis et filiabus nostris...” donated property to the monastery of San 
2 CONC Prudencio, for the souls of “...patris nostri Dni Semenez et Dnæ Mariæ uxoris eius”, by charter dated 29 Aug 1181[255].  Alfonso VIII King of Castile granted "el castillo de Isneda" to "Diego Ximénez señor de los Cameros" by chart
2 CONC er dated 9 Oct 1184[256]. 
2 CONT
