2 CONT Bernard-Roger of Foix
2 CONT
2 CONT and in French:  http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernard_Roger_de_Foix
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard Roger (c.962 – c.1034) was the count of Couserans, in which capacity he was lord of parts of Comminges  and Foix.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of count Roger I of Carcassonne. His elder brother, Raymond I of Carcassonne inherited the county of Carcassonne and the remaining part of the lordship of Comminges. Bernard Rogers comital status is attested in the 
2 CONC donation to the Abbey of Saint-Hilaire in 1011.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the founder of the House of Foix which ruled that county for centuries. During his father's lifetime, he married Arsinde, or Garsenda, the heiress of the county of Bigorre.
2 CONT
2 CONT He built the square tower of the castle at Foix in France and made it his capital, from which a town group up. He had endowed the monastery at Foix and in it he was buried when he died at the ripe old age of seventy-two.
2 CONT
2 CONT His lands were divided:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * His eldest son, Bernard of Foix, count of Bigorre, took the County of Bigorre.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * His second son, Roger I of Foix, count of Foix, became the first count of Foix, which included the castles of Castelpenent, Roquemaure, Lordat, and several within the county of Toulouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * His third and youngest son, Peter of Foix, lord of Couserans, inherited the lordship of Couserans.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT BERNARD ROGER de Carcassonne (summer 981-[22 Aug 1036/38]).  "Roggarius comes…cum coniuge comitissa Adalaice seu Regimundo sobole atque Bernardo sobole" donated property to the abbey of Saint-Hilaire by charter dated Aug 981[426].
2 CONC   “Rogerius comes”, under his testament dated to [1002], divided his properties, “ad Bernardo filio meo…comitatu de Cosoragno…castello de Fuxo”[427].  He succeeded in 1012 as Comte de Couserans and (part) Carcassonne, Seigneur du 
2 CONC pays de Foix.  He succeeded as Comte de Bigorre, de iure uxoris.     
2 CONT
2 CONT BERNARD ROGER de Carcassonne, son of ROGER [I] de Comminges Comte de Carcassonne & his wife Adelais de Pons (summer 981-[22 Aug 1036/38]).  "Roggarius comes…cum coniuge comitissa Adalaice seu Regimundo sobole atque Bernardo sobole
2 CONC " donated property to the abbey of Saint-Hilaire by charter dated Aug 981[858].  "Rotgerius comes et marchio cum coniuge comitissa Adalaisse atque cum prole Regimundo Barnardoque" donated property with the abbey of Saint-Hilaire b
2 CONC y charter dated 1 Nov 984[859].  "Rodgarius comes et uxor mea Aladaiz" donated property to the abbey of Lézat by charter dated Aug [1001], signed by "Ramundo, Bernardo, Petrone"[860].  “Rogerius comes”, under his testament dated t
2 CONC o [1002], divided his properties, “ad Bernardo filio meo…comitatu de Cosoragno…castello de Fuxo”[861].  "Rogerius comes et conjux mea Adalaizis comitissa" donated property to Saint-Hilaire, including property which "frater meus Od
2 CONC do comes habuit", for the soul of "fratris mei Oddoni comitis" and for "filio nostro Regimundo comite", by charter dated Apr 1011, signed by "…Bernardus et dominus Petrus…comites…"[862].  He succeeded in 1012 as Comte de Couserans
2 CONC  and (part) Carcassonne, Seigneur du pays de Foix.  Comte de Bigorre, by right of his wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1010]) GARSENDA Ctss de Bigorre, daughter of GARCIA ARNAUD Comte de Bigorre & his wife Ricarda --- ([986]-[1032/34]).  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 1034 under which “Rotgarius filius Garsente” paid homage to 
2 CONC “Petrone episcopo filio Adalais”[863].  The 15th century Chronicle of Esquerrier names "dona Beatriz de Bezes" as the wife of "Mossen Bernard"[864], but this source is too late to give much credibility to its account of the early 
2 CONC comtes de Foix.  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Bernard Roger & his wife had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         BERNARD de Foix (-before 24 Jun 1077).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Comte de Bigorre.    
