0 @N6000000002176683709@ NOTE As the kings of Leon expanded eastward, they reached Burgos. Because the area
1 CONT there was protected by castles built to guard the frontiers of the newly
1 CONT acquired territory, the region became know as Castilla, or Castile. Under
1 CONT Count Fernan Gonzales, the region became independent of Leon, and in 932
1 CONT Fernan declared himself first King of Castile. Later, Sancho, King of Navarre,
1 CONT captured much of Leon & Castile, and made son Ferdinand I King of Castile. On
1 CONT Sancho's death the kingdom was divided amongst his three sons - big trouble!
