1 CONT His father, Berenguer Ramon I (reigned 1018-35), divided and bequeathed his lands among his three sons; however, Sanç (or Sancho) in 1049 and Guillem (or William) in 1054 renounced their inheritances in their eldest brother's favo
1 CONC ur, thus reuniting the lands. Ramon Berenguer I also expanded his domain by securing control over the adjacent countiesof Ampurias and Pallars. His most noted achievement was convoking thelocal Cortes (assembly) and having it deli
1 CONC berate on a choice of Romanand medieval laws for Catalonia. The result was the promulgation of the celebrated legal code known as the Usatges de Barcelona
