0 @N6000000000943494701@ NOTE [Norvell.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [Nix.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [Nixon.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT Rodrigo Diaz (de Vivar), male line descendant (it would seem) of Judges Lain Calvo and Nuno Rasura, tracing back to a 9th century Nuno Belchidez.  In this descent, he was linked (in the male line) with to some of the early (non-he
1 CONC reditary) Counts of Castile, the Banu Gomez, the Banu Morel, and the Flainez/de Cifuentes families, and (in the female line) to the later (hereditary) Counts of Castile.  He married Jimena Diaz, a descendant of the 10th century co
1 CONC unt Piniolo Gundemariz.
0 @N6000000002176683876@ NOTE He was born as Rodigo de Vivar, son of a minor Castilian nobleman, though
1 CONT related on his mother's side to the "great landowing nobility", growing up in
1 CONT the household of a future king, Sancho II (c1038-1072). As a Spanish Warrior,
1 CONT he was at service to King Sancho II until he was assassinated, then offered
1 CONT his services to King Alfonso VI.
